---
/**
 * Loads a BRAND LAYER's element registry, so its playgrounds upgrade too.
 *
 * `LiveRuntime.astro` loads the shared library every design system is built
 * on. A design system may also declare a brand layer — a second package of
 * components belonging to it alone (`brandLibrary` in
 * `.altitude/ds-projects.json`) — and those elements live in a different
 * package, so they need a second import or their tags never upgrade.
 *
 * WHY THE SPECIFIER IS TYPED HERE, when nothing else about a design system is.
 * Everything else this site derives is DATA — a name, a route, a tag list — and
 * data can come from the registry. An import is not data: a bare specifier has
 * to be statically analysable for Vite to bundle it, and the package has to be
 * a real dependency of this app (apps/docs/package.json) before it can be
 * imported at all. A brand layer therefore costs one dependency and one line
 * here — unlike a whole design system, which still costs only a registry entry.
 * Shell.astro decides WHETHER to render this from `registry.layer`, so no page
 * pays for a layer it does not document, and no project id is branched on.
 *
 * Requires `window.alAutoRegistry = true` inline in <head> (Shell.astro) — the
 * layer's modules read it at module-eval time to decide whether to call
 * `customElements.define`, exactly as the base library's do (.altitude/REGISTRATION.md).
 */
---

<script>
  import '@southleft/sl-web-components';
</script>
